*widespread dissatisfaction**, not happiness.\n\n**6. People going about daily life activities with visible emotional states:**\n- The video does **not show many scenes of routine daily life** (e.g., shopping, working, commuting) with visible emotional states. Most scenes are either **protests, destruction, or social gatherings**. The **lack of “normal” daily life scenes** makes it difficult to claim general happiness.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe evidence across the 30 frames **does not support** the claim that “people living in Lebanon are happy about their life.” While **some individuals in specific moments (e.g., beach gathering) appear joyful**, the **dominant visual narrative** — protests, tear gas, economic graphs, destroyed infrastructure — reflects **frustration, anger, and hardship**.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should reflect **a complex, predominantly negative or conflicted attitude toward life**, not a simple “happy.”\n\n✅ **Final Verdict: The answer '1' is incorrect.**\n", "\n=== Batch 60-89 (29 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2008.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2009.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2010.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2011.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2012.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2013.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2014.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2015.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2016.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2017.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2018.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames/frame_2019.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/JPPMz8fEml0/frames